{
  "sources": [
    {
      "id": "HIS-PIGMENT-01",
      "title": "International Council of Museums: ICOM Code of Ethics for Museums (2017 edition)",
      "url": "https://icom.museum/wp-content/uploads/2018/07/ICOM-code-En-web.pdf",
      "locator": "Section 3.6, Destructive Analysis",
      "supports": "When destructive analysis is undertaken, the object record keeps track of the material analysed, the result and resulting research.",
      "accessed": "2026-11-26",
      "mla": {
        "kind": "page",
        "author": "International Council of Museums",
        "title": "ICOM Code of Ethics for Museums, 2017 edition",
        "container": "International Council of Museums"
      }
    }
  ],
  "dialogue": [
    {
      "id": "pigment-sample.window",
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "historicalLabel": "fictional-world",
      "text": "The borrowed strip is still sealed in Nell’s frame. Its older loan ticket says W27. The new workshop wrapper says R13. Its edge has two square notches where the display has one. Nell writes on the glass: please leave W27 whole, even at the corners.",
      "options": [
        {
          "text": "Match W27 to the loan ticket and R13 to the separate wrapper.",
          "if": {
            "objective": "pigment-window.controlled"
          },
          "effects": [
            {
              "setFlag": "pigment-sample.window",
              "value": true
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Read the museum guidance about keeping an analysis record.",
          "next": "pigment-sample.source"
        },
        {
          "text": "Leave the window sealed for now."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "pigment-sample.source",
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "historicalLabel": "documented",
      "text": "Museum conservation guidance calls for a permanent record of the material tested and what the analysis showed when testing uses up material. The record gives later researchers a way to tell exactly what was analysed.",
      "citationSource": "HIS-PIGMENT-01"
    },
    {
      "id": "pigment-sample.packet",
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "historicalLabel": "fictional-world",
      "text": "Nell’s signed R13 wrapper says this is the one loose practice swatch from a later batch. The workshop may use all of it for a material check, or return it whole to the window tray. The signature covers this wrapper alone. Both strips look violet in the window.",
      "options": [
        {
          "text": "Take the signed R13 wrapper with the loose swatch inside.",
          "if": {
            "all": [
              {
                "objective": "pigment-window.controlled"
              },
              {
                "flag": "pigment-sample.window",
                "eq": true
              },
              {
                "not": {
                  "flag": "pigment-sample.consent",
                  "eq": true
                }
              },
              {
                "not": {
                  "item": "item.pigment-sample.swatch"
                }
              },
              {
                "not": {
                  "flagSet": "pigment-sample.disposition"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          "effects": [
            {
              "setFlag": "pigment-sample.consent",
              "value": true
            },
            {
              "giveItem": "item.pigment-sample.swatch"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Leave the signed wrapper under the clip."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "pigment-sample.plan",
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "historicalLabel": "fictional-world",
      "text": "Oduya has kept one place for the report and one tray for the whole practice strip. The report could tell which kinds of colour were in R13. It would use up the only loose strip, so tomorrow’s visitor could not turn that edge under a lamp. If you keep it whole, tomorrow’s visitor can repeat the edge check and the workshop has no result about what is in the paint.",
      "options": [
        {
          "text": "Hand the signed R13 swatch to the workshop for the material report.",
          "if": {
            "all": [
              {
                "objective": "pigment-window.controlled"
              },
              {
                "flag": "pigment-sample.window",
                "eq": true
              },
              {
                "flag": "pigment-sample.consent",
                "eq": true
              },
              {
                "item": "item.pigment-sample.swatch"
              },
              {
                "not": {
                  "flagSet": "pigment-sample.disposition"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          "effects": [
            {
              "takeItem": "item.pigment-sample.swatch"
            },
            {
              "setFlag": "pigment-sample.disposition",
              "value": "analysis"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Set the signed R13 swatch in the comparison tray, still whole.",
          "if": {
            "all": [
              {
                "objective": "pigment-window.controlled"
              },
              {
                "flag": "pigment-sample.window",
                "eq": true
              },
              {
                "flag": "pigment-sample.consent",
                "eq": true
              },
              {
                "item": "item.pigment-sample.swatch"
              },
              {
                "not": {
                  "flagSet": "pigment-sample.disposition"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          "effects": [
            {
              "takeItem": "item.pigment-sample.swatch"
            },
            {
              "setFlag": "pigment-sample.disposition",
              "value": "retain"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Keep the wrapper in my bag and come back after a look at the window."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "pigment-sample.repair",
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "historicalLabel": "fictional-world",
      "text": "Someone has pencilled “Nell’s violet, now checked” over both clips. The runner thought the workshop slip and the borrowed display told the same story. Oduya asks you to give the next visitor a way to see where each claim begins and ends.",
      "options": [
        {
          "text": "Give W27 its own loan card and R13 its own record of what a reader can check.",
          "if": {
            "all": [
              {
                "objective": "pigment-sample.compared"
              },
              {
                "flag": "pigment-sample.disposition",
                "in": [
                  "analysis",
                  "retain"
                ]
              },
              {
                "flag": "pigment-sample.followed",
                "eq": true
              },
              {
                "not": {
                  "flag": "pigment-sample.posted",
                  "eq": true
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          "effects": [
            {
              "setFlag": "pigment-sample.posted",
              "value": true
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Leave the two clips visible and come back to the heading."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
